<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Avenue of the Dead</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Miccaotli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Avenue of the Dead is the main axis of Teotihuacan in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, a broad ceremonial way more than two kilometres long laid out in the early centuries CE. Running from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-the-moon">Pyramid of the Moon</a> past the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-the-sun">Pyramid of the Sun</a> to the Ciudadela, it is oriented about 15.5 degrees east of north. Its name was given by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a>, who believed the platforms lining it were tombs.</p></div>
